## Sources & references

The funnel framework as used here is the lineal descendant of the [AIDA model](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AIDA_(marketing)) (E. St. Elmo Lewis, 1898), updated through decades of marketing practice. The modern extension to post-purchase stages (retention, expansion) is broadly captured in the "pirate metrics" framework (AARRR) developed by Dave McClure at 500 Startups around 2007. CRO and funnel optimisation as a discipline owes much to [ConversionXL](https://cxl.com) and Andrew Chen's writing on growth at [andrewchen.com](https://andrewchen.com). David Skok's writing at [For Entrepreneurs](https://www.forentrepreneurs.com) on SaaS unit economics and acquisition is the canonical resource for the LTV / CAC / payback framing referenced throughout. The channel-saturation observation (paid channels getting more expensive over time) is widely documented; see e.g. WordStream's annual benchmark reports for Google Ads CPC trends. Specific Malaysian channel-fit patterns vary widely and should be triangulated with local industry data (e.g. iPrice, Statista Malaysia, GoBear-style market research).
